# Records, not points

Product law: `docs/design/Game_Design_Bible_v1.1.1.md`. On conflict the Bible wins. Laws 1, 2, 9. Audit V1, V2. Do not rebalance a points system.

## Banned — do not rebuild

No points, XP, currencies, dailies, streaks-as-economy, thresholds, engagement scores, contribution numbers, hours or combat-minutes, activity leaderboards, ELO/MMR, or Grant / standing / suggestion machinery.

Regression tells (grep; refuse and delete — do not rebalance): `standing`, `Grant`, `Grant(`, `threshold`, `suggestion`, `elo`, `leaderboard`, `prophet`.

## Ranks (exactly these; no thresholds)

Fresh Beef, Cooked Beef, Beef Knight, Beef Lord, Beef Butcher (raid-team role, display-only this phase), Beef Council. No Beef Prophet. The Pope is not a rank.

Attainment (§5, §10.4):

- **Fresh Beef** — recruitment (guild invite). This addon does not own recruit or purge.
- **Cooked Beef** — Discord/community step outside the addon; reflected when Council promotes.
- **Beef Knight** — Pope ceremony: KNIGHT THIS BEEF.
- **Beef Lord** — a Beef Knight who wins a sanctioned Gora the Pope judges fair; Pope elevates. Attainable.
- **Beef Butcher** — human raid-team designation. Display-only this phase.
- **Beef Council** — human judgment; prunable by the same judgment.

Ranks are relationships, not a linear ladder. After Lord: records, rivalries, defenses, narrative streaks, honorifics — not more ranks.

## Records are stories (§10.9)

Character-level: wins/losses, **sanctioned-Gora W/L streaks only** (narrative record, not an economy), defenses, head-to-heads, notable victims, rulings received. No damage meters, duration stats, or per-class win rates. Engagement, login, daily, favor, and accuracy streaks remain banned (§4.6, §10.6).

**Records Book** = parchment superlatives, not a sortable ranked ladder. Bible MVP categories (veto: OPEN_QUESTIONS #3): Most Sanctioned Victories; Longest Streak; Most Successful Defenses; The Iron Chin; Greatest Rivalry; Famous Upsets (Pope-flagged); The Undefeated; The Glorious Martyr; Tournament Champions.

## Recognition (§15, §17)

- Honorifics: Pope-granted, named, cosmetic text only. No mechanical benefits.
- Quiet Knights: witnessed history plus human recognition. No service scores, no achievement tracks.
- Different contributions stay distinguishable — no single number may collapse them.
- Record events, never behavior. No activity leaderboards. Ever.

Do not invent product answers. Unanswered items go to `docs/design/OPEN_QUESTIONS.md`.
